# Build output
/target

# Release artefacts. build-installer.cmd regenerates dist/PadForge-Setup.exe.
/dist

# The scratch copy make_icon.py writes. The ICO that windres reads is
# tools/padforge.ico, which is committed: CI has no Python with Pillow, so the
# build has to work from a file that is actually in the repository.
tools/assets/

# Debug screenshots taken next to the source during development.
*.log
docs/*.png
# Automation scratch: _shot_pw.ps1 / _pulse.ps1 capture PNGs named _shot_* and
# _pulse* while driving the real window. They are a diagnostic, not a build
# input, so the captures are disposable and the scripts stay.
tools/_shot_*.png
tools/_pulse*.png
# ...except the ones the README and the release page show.
!docs/installer.png
!docs/icon-128.png
!docs/icon-512.png
!docs/icon-sizes.png
# The UI screenshots are documentation, not development debris: a README whose
# pictures only exist on the machine that wrote it is a README with holes in it.
!docs/ui-*.png

# Binaries and debug symbols
*.exe
*.pdb
*.dll
*.rlib

# Editor and OS noise
**/*.rs.bk
*~
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
desktop.initools/_commit_msg.txt
